fxtranslate (engine for automatic translation of descriptions)
--------------------------------------------------------------
https://crates.io/crates/fxtranslate (version 0.4.2)
Repository in the crate metadata: https://github.com/gregtatum/translations
(directory inference-rs/crates/fxtranslate of the inference-rs branch)
License: MPL-2.0

Use in Rexon:
  * Automatic translation of theme descriptions (en→ru) is done by a Rust
    implementation of the Firefox translation engine. The crate is VENDORED
    into the tree (rust/vendor/fxtranslate/crate — byte for byte the archive
    published on crates.io, sha256 pinned in scripts/sync-fxtranslate.py) and
    linked statically into the core; the vendored copy is rebuilt with the
    same single command.
  * Our changes to the crate are kept in ONE file,
    rust/vendor/fxtranslate/patches/0001-*.patch, and they touch six files:
    build.rs, src/engine.rs, src/gemm.rs, src/gemmology_shim.cpp,
    src/ops.rs, src/shortlist.rs. The main ones are choosing the instruction
    set by CPUID (without it the engine dies with SIGILL on x86-64 without
    AVX2, and only after the model has loaded) and a fix for the first
    decoding token.
  * MPL-2.0 is a PER-FILE copyleft: it covers the files of the crate itself
    that we changed, not the rest of Rexon's code (Apache-2.0) that links
    against it. The duty to "publish the sources of the changed files" is met
    by publishing that very patch: the package installs it as
    /usr/share/licenses/rexon-git/fxtranslate-0.4.2-rexon.patch next to the
    license text (LICENSE.fxtranslate-MPL-2.0).
  * The download/net/discovery features are NOT enabled: the engine makes no
    network requests, the model is fixed in the shipped build.
  Full MPL-2.0 text: rust/vendor/fxtranslate/crate/LICENSE.
  Obligations and the vendoring procedure:
  rust/vendor/fxtranslate/ATTRIBUTION.md.

